 "bindingConditions": [
  {
   "id": "C2",
   "binding": "CONSUMER_CONDITION_FOR_ACCEPTANCE",
   "text": "While a result has planValidity REQUIRES_RECONCILIATION (a pending UNREPORTED_TRAINING question, a HOLD such as R4, or a clinical dependency), no consumer presents the stored run doses ahead as a prescription. The question, and any strength change kept beside it, are the only actionable items. Carry this in the freeze record and the handoff."
  },
  {
   "id": "C3",
   "binding": "G03_CONDITION_FOR_USE_BEYOND_OFFLINE_REFERENCE",
   "text": "The answer path is low-friction and factual: done or not done per session, or a declared break with its reason, screened clinically. HealthKit evidence is used before asking where available. Non-response never falls back silently to credit or zero. While referenceState.pending.signal is present, the answer is delivered as a plain review of that week or as the pending event kind with its signals. An answer inside another event kind is followed by the held signal re-submitted before the plan is presented. A RECOVERED event does not carry the answer (it stays ASK). After a clinical route, the answer is kept and re-sent, or asked again, after qualified clearance (R5). Cadence and wording belong to G03."
  },
  {
   "id": "C7",
   "binding": "DISCLOSURE",
   "text": "The closure records the following as disclosed residuals, with this record's corrections. D1. B2. The B1 observation. The ratified fifth fixture. R1 at its measured magnitude (up to EASY 50 / QUALITY 34 / LONG 55, and a race touch in race week, until the next decision). R2 with A* as the only differing reference. R3 persisting one step into the following week. R4. R5. The SD-03 non-review route (SSCTR-SD5-02)."
  },
  {
   "id": "C8",
   "binding": "CONSUMER_CONDITION_FOR_ACCEPTANCE (via C3) and NON_BLOCKING_NEXT_RUNTIME_REVISION (engine)",
   "text": "Engine, in the next runtime revision: a held reactive signal is never cleared without being re-evaluated. Any decision that answers the question either re-evaluates it, or keeps it pending with the plan REQUIRES_RECONCILIATION until the signal kind is re-submitted, or at least discloses it. Until then, the consumer obligation in C3 applies."
  },
  {
   "id": "C9",
   "binding": "CONSUMER_CONDITION_FOR_ACCEPTANCE; ENGINEERING_BEFORE_ANY_USE_BEYOND_THE_OFFLINE_REFERENCE",
   "text": "This applies after an answer to UNREPORTED_TRAINING that leaves sessions of the answer week elapsed before it, including the taper-to-race-week case. The following week's conditional projection is not presented or delivered as a prescription until a decision re-plans it: the answer week's review, or the first decision of the next week. The client triggers that decision at the week boundary. Carry this in the freeze record and the handoff, as C2 is carried. Engineering, before any use beyond the offline reference: re-project later weeks without crediting those elapsed unreported sessions (read them as unknown), or mark the projection as conditional on the week's review. Add a directed test that pins week b+1 after a day-2 known-stop answer."
  }
 ],
